From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Attard <sattard@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 18:48:22 +0000
Subject: feat: add NetworkContextParams::block_network

Adds a per-NetworkContext switch that refuses every network connection for
the context. When set, URL loads for non-local schemes, WebSockets,
WebTransport sessions, preconnects, prefetches and host resolutions fail
with ERR_NETWORK_ACCESS_REVOKED; the raw TCP/UDP, proxy-resolving, P2P and
mDNS socket interfaces are not bound; and all host mapping is set to
^NOTFOUND so code built directly on the URLRequestContext (cert fetching,
reporting) cannot reach the network either.

Electron uses this to implement sessions created with
`networkAccess: 'none'`, which must be fully offline regardless of which
browser-side path created the request.

